  "term": "Grooved Pegboard Test",
  "definition": "The Grooved Pegboard Test is a hand-use dexterity test that uses a pegboard with 25 specially shaped pegs placed into holes. It is used to assess manipulative skill and can be particularly useful in detecting one-sided brain damage.",
